---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Media from '../components/Media.astro';
import Colophon from '../components/Colophon.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { getPublishedPosts } from '../lib/writing';

const showWriting = (await getPublishedPosts()).length > 0;
const access = site.links.edgarMiner ?? `mailto:${site.email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('Edgar Miner access')}`;
const accessText = site.links.edgarMiner ? 'Try it.' : 'Ask for access.';
---
<Base title={site.name} description={site.tagline}>
  <Nav slot="nav" showWriting={showWriting} />
  <section class="intro">
    <h1>Hi, I'm Chandni.</h1>
    <p class="purpose">{site.tagline}</p>

    <p>Right now I'm building <a href="/work/edgar-miner/">Edgar Miner</a> at ThinkMocha. It reads every SEC filing so you don't have to. <a href={access}>{accessText}</a></p>

    {site.hero && <Media items={[site.hero]} />}

    <p>In 2022 my daughter was three and would not eat vegetables. One night I used AI to make her a storybook where she was the hero and the vegetables were part of the adventure. She cleared her plate.</p>

    <p>That turned into ThinkMocha: AI-personalized books for kids, with characters who look like them and stories from their own cultures. I built the whole thing myself and ran a pilot that put <a href="/work/thinkmocha/">50+ books</a> into a Manhattan preschool. 90%+ of parents and teachers asked for more.</p>

    <p>Before that I spent six years as a backend engineer. At Rakuten I led backend for <a href="https://www.rakuten.com/dining">Rakuten Dining</a>, a rewards product with 10,000+ restaurants, and ran the serverless proof of concept that cut the company's infrastructure costs 80%. At Serverless I rebuilt billing on Stripe and cut processing time 98%. Before any of that I shipped a Chrome extension that TechCrunch wrote about.</p>

    <p>Did a bunch of other stuff too.</p>

    <p>Built <a href="/work/fundraising-agent/">Fundraising Agent</a>, an AI agent that runs investor outreach for founders and takes it from 20 hours a week to under 2; built an events app that never got past my friends; won three hackathons with an image-recognition shopping app, an event discovery platform, and an Arduino scoring system; got a Tech MBA from NYU Stern in 2026 while doing the above, and screened deep-tech startups for its accelerator on the side; apply to YC every year.</p>

    <p class="lines">
      Some of it worked.<br />
      Most of it didn't.<br />
      {site.links.ideas
        ? <>Entrepreneurs aren't defined by their first 87 ideas. <a href={site.links.ideas}>Here are mine.</a></>
        : <>Entrepreneurs aren't defined by their first 87 ideas.</>}
    </p>

    <p>I also speak five languages, which is a better conversation starter than anything above.</p>

    <p class="ps">P.S. Email me at <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. Short emails with a clear ask get answers.</p>
  </section>
  <Colophon slot="colophon" />
</Base>
